/-- Convergence of the covariance (thesis Prop. 4.7). Let $(\gamma_x)$ be cell data on the chain
with one mode per site and $\gamma^{(t)} = (L_{\varphi, \lambda*})^t \gamma$ the cells evolved $t$
times. For all real $\varphi$, $\lambda$, $k$ and $t \in \mathbb N$,
$\hat\gamma^{(t)}(k) = (\hat L(k)^t)^T\, \hat\gamma(k)\, \hat L(k)^t$. If $(\varphi, \lambda)$ lies
in the regime, then for every site $x$ and every entry, $(\gamma^{(t)}_x)_{ab}$ converges to the
corresponding entry of the limit cell $\gamma_{\infty, x}$, and for all vectors $u$, $w$ of the
lattice phase space the forms converge, $\gamma^{(t)}(u, w) \to \gamma_\infty(u, w)$, where
$\gamma_\infty$ is the form of the limit cells. -/
theorem dyn_tendsto_cells {φ lam : ℝ}
    {γc : ℤ → Matrix (Gaussian.PhaseIndex 1) (Gaussian.PhaseIndex 1) ℝ} (h : CellData γc) :
    (∀ (t : ℕ) (k : ℝ), gammaHat ((evolveCells (rotationSymbol φ lam))^[t] γc) k =
      ((exampleSymbol φ lam k ^ t)ᵀ).map Complex.ofReal * gammaHat γc k *
        (exampleSymbol φ lam k ^ t).map Complex.ofReal) ∧
    (ExampleRegime φ lam →
      (∀ x a b, Tendsto (fun t : ℕ => (evolveCells (rotationSymbol φ lam))^[t] γc x a b) atTop
        (𝓝 (limitCells φ lam γc x a b))) ∧
      ∀ u w : Core.LatticeSpace ℝ ℤ (Gaussian.PhaseIndex 1),
        Tendsto (fun t : ℕ => cellForm ((evolveCells (rotationSymbol φ lam))^[t] γc) u w) atTop
          (𝓝 (cellForm (limitCells φ lam γc) u w))) := sorry

